# Markdown YAML frontmatter

When creating or editing a `.md` file, start it with YAML frontmatter so the user has context at a glance.

Keep it short. Put the frontmatter first, then a blank line, then the body.

```markdown
---
title: Hello
description: Demo file for the Cursor sandbox.
audience: beginners
status: draft
---

# Hello

This file is the demo.
```

Required fields:

- `title`: short name of the doc
- `description`: one sentence on what it is for

Optional fields when they help:

- `audience`: who this is for
- `status`: `draft` or `ready`

Do not invent extra metadata. Do not wrap existing docs in frontmatter unless the user asked or you are creating a new `.md` file.
